\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Mean accuracy degradation (baseline minus post-drift accuracy) by model, per dataset. Random Forest's advantage over LightGBM holds in direction across all three datasets. Logistic Regression's poor aggregate performance is driven almost entirely by Telco Churn, where it is the least robust model by a wide margin; on the other two datasets it is competitive with or better than both ensembles.}}{4}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:modelrobustness}{{5}{4}{Mean accuracy degradation (baseline minus post-drift accuracy) by model, per dataset. Random Forest's advantage over LightGBM holds in direction across all three datasets. Logistic Regression's poor aggregate performance is driven almost entirely by Telco Churn, where it is the least robust model by a wide margin; on the other two datasets it is competitive with or better than both ensembles}{figure.5}{}}
